WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.380
But they go to Florida, Miami . . . on a Friday night in Miami and beat a pretty good ball club.

2
00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:21.680
Miami, at that time, was recruiting kids from all over the country, primarily from Pennsylvania, New Jersey, some from Florida.

3
00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:28.340
But they were . . . They had some big linemen from everywhere, you know.

4
00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:36.760
And they had what I would call an established national program.

5
00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:40.000
LSU beat them 41–0.

6
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:47.900
So that Monday, the following Monday, LSU’s ranked 9th in the AP Poll.

7
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:50.760
Dave Garroway was the host of “The Today Show.”

8
00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:59.500
Well, NBC Sports had the rights to the college football, so as a gimmick to hype their football property,

9
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:04.880
“The Today Show” came out with their rankings every Monday morning, you know.

10
00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:08.760
LSU’s ranked ninth in the country by “The Today Show.”

11
00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:10.660
AP did the same thing.

12
00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:18.920
So that morning when I went to work, I couldn’t find a parking place! [laughs] All the places were taken.

13
00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:22.200
There was a campus policeman out there directing traffic.

14
00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:26.020
There was a line around the stadium and it wasn’t eight o’clock yet, you know.

15
00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:29.480
I mean, they hadn’t even opened the ticket office.

16
00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:31.080
So this was a first, you know.

17
00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:34.960
All of the sudden, you know, the bandwagon was getting crowded.
